{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "c8f0d3b2-5a7e-4f4b-8d9c-3b2e6a8f0d12",
    "name": "ReadMeAI API — Server Routes",
    "description": "🛠 **ReadMeAI Server — API Test Collection**\n\nLives with the backend code (`server/postman/postman.json`) so anyone working on the Express API can test **every** route immediately.\n\n**Stack:** Node.js + Express 4 (ESM, TypeScript) · MongoDB (Mongoose 8) · OpenAI Chat Completions (`gpt-4o-mini`) · JWT httpOnly cookie auth · GitHub OAuth.\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 Quick start\n```bash\ncd server\ncp .env.example .env   # fill MONGO_URI, JWT_SECRET (OPENAI_API_KEY optional)\nnpm run seed           # demo data + demo user (optional)\nnpm run dev            # listens on http://localhost:4000\n```\n\n### 🔑 Auth flow\n1. Run **Auth → Login (Demo User)** — the test script grabs the `readmeai_token` cookie and stores it in `{{token}}`.\n2. Every protected request sends `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}` automatically (collection-level auth). The server also accepts the raw cookie, so cookie-jar requests work too.\n3. For **🛡 Admin** routes, run **Auth → Login (Admin)** first (`requireAuth` + `requireAdmin`).\n\n### 📌 Variables\n| Variable | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| `baseUrl` | API origin — default `http://localhost:4000` (change for Render preview URLs) |\n| `token` | JWT — auto-saved by Login/Register test scripts |\n| `readmeId` | Saved by **Generate README** |\n| `sessionId` | Chat session id (`postman-session-1`) |\n| `notificationId` / `issueId` / `adminIssueId` | Auto-saved from list/create responses |\n\n> Demo → `demo@readmeai.dev / demo123456` · Admin → `admin@readmeai.local / admin12345`",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "readmeai-server"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
