        {
          "name": "OAuth Callback",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/github/callback?code=REAL_CODE_FROM_GITHUB&state=REAL_STATE",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "github",
                "callback"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "code",
                  "value": "REAL_CODE_FROM_GITHUB",
                  "description": "One-time code GitHub appended to the redirect URI"
                },
                {
                  "key": "state",
                  "value": "REAL_STATE",
                  "description": "State issued by /connect (valid 10 minutes, single use)"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "**GET /api/github/callback**\n\nGitHub's redirect target. Exchanges `code` → token, fetches the GitHub user, links (or creates) the app user, sets `readmeai_token`, then redirects to `CLIENT_ORIGIN/auth/callback?github=success` (or `?github=error`).\n\nReplayed/fake `state` is rejected — test the real flow through a browser."
